{"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/SpectralGraphTheory\/documentation\/SpectralGraphTheory\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/numberOfSpanningTrees(weight:)-28jjs"},"metadata":{"roleHeading":"Instance Method","role":"symbol","symbolKind":"method","modules":[{"name":"SpectralGraphTheory","relatedModules":["GraphProtocols"]}],"externalID":"s:14GraphProtocols0A0P08SpectralA6TheoryE21numberOfSpanningTrees6weightSdqd__5Edges_5IndexQZXE_tSBRd__lF","remoteSource":{"fileName":"ElectricalNetworks.swift","url":"https:\/\/github.com\/Tyler-Keith-Thompson\/Grafluent\/blob\/main\/Sources\/SpectralGraphTheory\/ElectricalNetworks.swift#L64"},"title":"numberOfSpanningTrees(weight:)","extendedModule":"GraphProtocols","fragments":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"numberOfSpanningTrees","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"W","kind":"genericParameter"},{"text":">(","kind":"text"},{"text":"weight","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": (","kind":"text"},{"text":"Self","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":".","kind":"text"},{"text":"Edges","preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols0A0P5EdgesQa","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":".","kind":"text"},{"text":"Index","preciseIdentifier":"s:Sl5IndexQa","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":") -> ","kind":"text"},{"text":"W","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":") -> ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Double","preciseIdentifier":"s:Sd","kind":"typeIdentifier"}]},"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The number of spanning trees τ(G), weighted: the sum over spanning trees of the product of"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"their weights, which is any cofactor of the Laplacian (Kirchhoff’s matrix-tree theorem)."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Loops never lie on a tree; parallel edges each count. 0 for the empty graph and for a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"disconnected one, 1 for one vertex. NetworkX "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"number_of_spanning_trees"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"tokens":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"numberOfSpanningTrees"},{"kind":"text","text":"<"},{"kind":"genericParameter","text":"W"},{"kind":"text","text":">("},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"weight"},{"kind":"text","text":": ("},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Self"},{"kind":"text","text":"."},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols0A0P5EdgesQa","text":"Edges","identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/Edges-swift.associatedtype"},{"kind":"text","text":"."},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:Sl5IndexQa","text":"Index"},{"kind":"text","text":") -> "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"W"},{"kind":"text","text":") -> "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:Sd","text":"Double"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"where"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"W"},{"kind":"text","text":" : "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:SB","text":"BinaryFloatingPoint"}],"languages":["swift"],"platforms":["Linux"]}]},{"content":[{"level":2,"type":"heading","text":"Discussion","anchor":"discussion"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"A ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Double"},{"text":": counts pass ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Int"},{"text":" quickly (K₂₅ has 25²³). The Laplacian with one vertex removed","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"is eliminated densely as Grassmann, Taksar and Heyman eliminate (each pivot a sum of","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"conductances, never a difference), so the count keeps a relative accuracy of about n · 10⁻¹⁶","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"whatever the weights; its pivots are multiplied with the binary exponent kept apart, so it","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"overflows only past ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Double"},{"text":"’s range, to ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".infinity"},{"text":". When every weight is an integer","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"(unweighted included) and the count is below 2¹⁰⁰, it is computed exactly instead (two","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"determinants modulo 62-bit primes, combined by the Chinese remainder theorem) and rounded","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"once, so a count below 2⁵³ is exact. O(n³) time (less on sparse graphs), n² ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Double"},{"text":"s.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"weight","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" gives the weight of the edge at each position, read once per position; a weight of","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"0 is no edge.","type":"text"}]},{"style":"note","name":"Precondition","type":"aside","content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Every weight is finite and nonnegative."}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"kind":"content"}],"sections":[],"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"major":0,"patch":0},"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/spectralgraphtheory\/graphprotocols\/graph\/numberofspanningtrees(weight:)-28jjs"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"kind":"symbol","hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/SpectralGraphTheory\/documentation\/SpectralGraphTheory","doc:\/\/SpectralGraphTheory\/documentation\/SpectralGraphTheory\/GraphProtocols","doc:\/\/SpectralGraphTheory\/documentation\/SpectralGraphTheory\/GraphProtocols\/Graph"]]},"references":{"doc://GraphProtocols/documentation/GraphProtocols/Graph/Edges-swift.associatedtype":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/Edges-swift.associatedtype","fragments":[{"text":"associatedtype","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Edges","kind":"identifier"},{"text":" : ","kind":"te